		    <abstract language="eng">
		    	<p>We address data assimilation for linear and nonlinear dynamical systems via the so-called <i>model reference adaptive system</i>. Continuing our theoretical developments in [<span class="xref"><a href="#b25" ref-type="bibr">25</a></span>], we deliver the first practical implementation of this approach for online parameter identification with time series data. Our semi-implicit scheme couples a modified state equation with a parameter evolution law that is driven by model-data residuals. We demonstrate four benchmark problems of increasing complexity: The Darcy flow, the Fisher-KPP equation, a nonlinear potential equation, and, finally, an Allen–Cahn-type equation. Across all cases, explicit model reference adaptive system construction, verified assumptions, and numerically stable reconstructions underline our proposed method as a reliable, versatile tool for data assimilation and real-time inversion.</p>
		    </abstract>
